From 964bac6bde7ffbb88bbe71083f39687ad7bafe13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michael=20Wei=C3=9F?= <michael.weiss@aisec.fraunhofer.de>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 09:18:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: lx2160a: enable crypto device node for CAAM
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

To allow CAAM to work, e.g. for trusted keys, we have to
enable the corresponding device node.

Signed-off-by: Michael Weiß <michael.weiss@aisec.fraunhofer.de>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/fsl-lx2160a-tqmlx2160a.dtsi | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/fsl-lx2160a-tqmlx2160a.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/fsl-lx2160a-tqmlx2160a.dtsi
index 89a4765737b4..0341849560e2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/fsl-lx2160a-tqmlx2160a.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/fsl-lx2160a-tqmlx2160a.dtsi
@@ -95,3 +95,11 @@ eeprom2: eeprom@50 {
 		vcc-supply = <&reg_vcc3v3>;
 	};
 };
+
+&crypto {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&sec_jr3 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
-- 
2.47.3

